  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The United States recently experienced a wave of technical disruptions affecting various sectors, including banking, air travel, and national security systems. In response to these events, Senator Marco Rubio clarified that officials had found no evidence suggesting the incidents were part of a coordinated cyberattack or a systemic assault on the nation. Other reports indicated that officials briefed Congress, identifying failures in artificial intelligence systems as a factor in outages at institutions like JPMorgan, Microsoft, and the NSA. Amid the resulting public uncertainty, some consumers have begun stockpiling supplies. Following the criticism regarding the management of these technical failures, the White House confirmed the departure of Sean Cairncross from his position as national cyber director. Kirsten Davies, an official from the Department of Defense, has been appointed to take over the role as the government continues to manage the fallout from the infrastructure instability.",
